The runtime exception occurred because R8/ProGuard shrinks and strips generic signatures (`Signature` attribute) and anonymous subclasses of `TypeToken` during release builds (`isMinifyEnabled = true`), preventing Gson from resolving the generic type argument `List<Book>` at runtime. Additionally, R8 would obfuscate the model fields needed for deserialization.

The fix has been added to [proguard-rules.pro](file:///mnt/01DC198BE9192500/github/Schooldev/3S-study-work/trials/e4/c4-agy-B-r3/work/app/proguard-rules.pro):

```pro
# Preserve generic type signatures and annotations for reflection (Gson TypeToken)
-keepattributes Signature
-keepattributes *Annotation*

# Gson TypeToken rules for R8 / ProGuard
-keep class com.google.gson.reflect.TypeToken { *; }
-keep class * extends com.google.gson.reflect.TypeToken
-keepclassmembers class * extends com.google.gson.reflect.TypeToken {
    <init>(...);
}

# Preserve model classes so Gson can serialize/deserialize fields via reflection
-keep class vn.shelftap.lab.model.** { *; }
-keepclassmembers class vn.shelftap.lab.model.** { *; }
```
